# Experiment 3 — CI/CD Pipeline Java Maven Project with Kubernetes

## 1. Create Project Folder

```bash
mkdir java-kubernetes-app
cd java-kubernetes-app
```

---

## 2. Create Maven Folder Structure

```bash
mkdir -p src/main/java/com/example
```

Project structure:

```text
java-kubernetes-app
│── pom.xml
│── Dockerfile
│── Jenkinsfile
│── deployment.yaml
│── service.yaml
└── src
    └── main
        └── java
            └── com
                └── example
                    └── App.java
```

---

## 3. Create Java File

```bash
nano src/main/java/com/example/App.java
```

Paste:

```java
package com.example;

public class App {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Application Deployed Successfully on Kubernetes");
    }
}
```

Save:

```text
CTRL + O
Enter
CTRL + X
```

---

## 4. Create pom.xml

```bash
nano pom.xml
```

Paste:

```xml
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>java-kubernetes-app</artifactId>
    <version>1.0</version>

    <properties>
        <maven.compiler.source>17</maven.compiler.source>
        <maven.compiler.target>17</maven.compiler.target>
    </properties>
</project>
```

---

## 5. Build Maven Project

```bash
mvn clean package
```

This creates:

```text
target/java-kubernetes-app-1.0.jar
```

---

## 6. Run Java Program

```bash
java -cp target/java-kubernetes-app-1.0.jar com.example.App
```

Output:

```text
Application Deployed Successfully on Kubernetes
```

---

## 7. Create Dockerfile

```bash
nano Dockerfile
```

Paste:

```dockerfile
FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jdk

WORKDIR /app

COPY target/java-kubernetes-app-1.0.jar app.jar

CMD ["java","-cp","app.jar","com.example.App"]
```

---

## 8. Build Docker Image

```bash
docker build -t yourdockerhubusername/java-kubernetes-app:v1 .
```

---

## 9. Login to Docker Hub

```bash
docker login
```

Enter your Docker Hub username and password.

---

## 10. Push Docker Image

```bash
docker push yourdockerhubusername/java-kubernetes-app:v1
```

---

## 11. Initialize Git

```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Java Kubernetes Project"
```

---

## 12. Push to GitHub

Create an empty GitHub repository.

Then execute:

```bash
git branch -M main
git remote add origin YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL
git push -u origin main
```

---

## 13. Start Kubernetes Cluster

If using Minikube:

```bash
minikube start
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get nodes
```

---

## 14. Create Kubernetes Deployment File

```bash
nano deployment.yaml
```

Paste:

```yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: java-app

spec:
  replicas: 2

  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: java-app

  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: java-app

    spec:
      containers:
      - name: java-app
        image: yourdockerhubusername/java-kubernetes-app:v1
```

---

## 15. Create Kubernetes Service File

```bash
nano service.yaml
```

Paste:

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service

metadata:
  name: java-service

spec:
  selector:
    app: java-app

  ports:
  - port: 8080
    targetPort: 8080

  type: NodePort
```

---

## 16. Deploy Application to Kubernetes

```bash
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
```

---

## 17. Create Kubernetes Service

```bash
kubectl apply -f service.yaml
```

---

## 18. Verify Deployment

```bash
kubectl get all
```

---

## 19. Access Application

```bash
minikube service java-service --url
```

---

## 20. Create Jenkinsfile

```bash
nano Jenkinsfile
```

Paste:

```groovy
pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {

        stage('Build Maven') {
            steps {
                sh 'mvn clean package'
            }
        }

        stage('Build Docker Image') {
            steps {
                sh 'docker build -t yourdockerhubusername/java-kubernetes-app:v1 .'
            }
        }

        stage('Push Docker Image') {
            steps {
                sh 'docker push yourdockerhubusername/java-kubernetes-app:v1'
            }
        }

        stage('Deploy Kubernetes') {
            steps {
                sh 'kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml'
                sh 'kubectl apply -f service.yaml'
            }
        }

    }
}
```

---

## 21. Push Jenkinsfile to GitHub

```bash
git add .
git commit -m "Added Jenkins Pipeline"
git push
```

---

## 22. Jenkins Execution Steps

1. Open Jenkins.
2. Click **New Item**.
3. Enter name: `java-kubernetes-pipeline`
4. Select **Pipeline**.
5. Click **OK**.
6. Go to **Pipeline** section.
7. Select **Pipeline script from SCM**.
8. SCM: **Git**
9. Paste your GitHub repository URL.
10. Branch: `main`
11. Script Path: `Jenkinsfile`
12. Click **Save**.
13. Click **Build Now**.

